          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#CoveringAnAffineSymplecticGroup Covering an affine symplectic group
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+space"} symplectic vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\omega)
            one may consider the restriction of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+group"} quantomorphism group
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+symplectic+group"} affine symplectic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ASp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ASp(V,\omega)
            (
            %a{:href => "#RobbinSalamon93"}> Robbin-Salamon 93, corollary 9.3
            )
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ESp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi QuantMorph
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ASp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi HamSympl
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  ESp(V,\omega) &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; QuantMorph(V,\omega)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  ASp(V,\omega)
                  \&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;
                  HamSympl(V,\omega)
                  }
          %p
            Sometimes (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#RobbinSalamon93"} Robbin-Salamon 93, p. 30
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ESp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ESp(V,\omega)
            is called the
            = succeed "," do
              %em extended symplectic group
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+affine+symplectic+group"} extended affine symplectic group
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#ARZ06"} ARZ 06, prop. V.1
          %p
            Notice that the further restriction to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            regarded as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/translation+group"} translation group
            over itself is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+group"} Heisenberg group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Heis
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Heis(V,\omega)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Heis
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi ESp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi QuantMorph
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
