          %h2#References References
          %h3#general General
          %p Original accounts are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marie+Souriau"}> Jean-Marie Souriau
                ,
                %em Structure des systemes dynamiques
                Dunod, Paris (1970)
              %p Translated and reprinted as (see section V.18 for the quantomorphism group):
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marie+Souriau"}> Jean-Marie Souriau
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Structure of dynamical systems - A symplectic view of physics
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-0281-3"} 10.1007/978-1-4612-0281-3
            %li#Kostant
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertram+Kostant"}> Bertram Kostant
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantization and unitary representations
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Lectures in modern analysis and applications III
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0079068"} 10.1007/BFb0079068
          %p A textbook account is in
          %ul
            %li#Brylinski93
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Luc+Brylinski"}> Jean-Luc Brylinski
              , section II.4
              = succeed "," do
                %em Loop spaces, characteristic classes and geometric quantization
          %p and in
          %ul
            %li
              Rudolf Schmid,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Infinite-dimensional Lie groups with applications to mathematical physics
              %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jgsp/1495505067"} Project Euclid
          %p
            The description in terms of automorphism in the slice
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul
            %li#FRS13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"} Chris Rogers
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+geometric+prequantum+theory"} Higher geometric prequantum theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1304.0236"}> arXiv:1304.0236
              )
          %p and in section 4.4.17 of
          %ul
            %li#Sch
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %p Another expository account, which spells out the details of the isomorphism from smooth functions with the Poisson bracket to infinitesimal quantomorphisms is given in
          %ul
            %li
              %span.newWikiWord>
                Jennifer Vaughan
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Jennifer+Vaughan"} ?
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://hdl.handle.net/1807/77389"} Quantomorphisms and Quantized Energy Levels for Metaplectic-c Quantization
          %h3#SmoothManifoldStructure Smooth manifold structure
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+group"} diffeological group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+group"} smooth group
            structure) on the quantomorphism group is at least implicit in
          %ul
            %li#Souriau79
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marie+Souriau"}> Jean-Marie Souriau
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Groupes différentiels
              %em Differential Geometrical Methods in Mathematical Physics
              (Proc. Conf., Aix-en-Provence/Salamanca, 1979), Lecture Notes in Math. 836, Springer, Berlin, (1980), pp. 91–128. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=607688"}> MathSciNet
              )
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ILH+manifold"} ILH group
            structure on the quantomorphism group is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Omori
              %p
                H. Omori,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Infinite dimensional Lie transformation groups
            %li#RatiuSchmid
              %p
                T. Ratiu, R. Schmid,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The differentiable structure of three remarkable diffeomorphism groups
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+manifold"} regular convenient Lie group
            structure is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Vizman
              Cornelia Vizman,
              %em Some remarks on the quantomorphism group
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/VizmanQuantomorphism.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            A
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric"} metric
          %ul
            %li
              Y. Eliashberg,; L. Polterovich,
              = succeed "." do
                %em Partially ordered groups and geometry of contact transformations
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/PL00001656"} 10.1007/PL00001656
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9910065"} math/9910065
          %h3#examples_2 Examples
          %p
            The quantomorphisms over elements of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+group"} symplectic group
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+space"} symplectic vector space
            are discussed in
          %ul
